// `FormData`'s constructor takes an `HTMLFormElement` to read initial entries
// from, and a submitter button beside it. Neither exists off the browser, and
// naming them would make `web:file` import `web:dom`. Every program that
// reaches a file would then load the whole DOM.
//
// The no-argument form is what every environment has, and what a browser
// program writes unless it is populating from a form element. That case loses
// its constructor, which is what the portable form costs.
//
// `@env` does not reach it. Upstream declares one constructor with both
// parameters optional, so restoring it needs either per-parameter availability
// or a constructor overload set, and the overlay rejects a second constructor
// under one name. #1613 has the detail.
export declare class FormData {
    constructor(mut self),
}
